=== Changes from v3.2 ===
  v3.2 cells: 18 (4 AND, 4 DFF_PN0, 2 DLATCH, 5 NOT, 3 OR)
  v3.3 cells: 18 (4 AND, 4 DFF_PN0, 2 DLATCH, 5 NOT, 3 OR)
  Change: std_cell_clk_or replaces std_cell_or.
  Net cell count unchanged (std_cell_clk_or maps to same $_OR_ primitive).
  Structural improvement: clk_out driven by clock-domain-aware OR gate.

=== Notes ===
- All 4 DFFs are INTENTIONAL: they form the 2-stage synchronizer chains in
  std_cell_sync instances (u_sync_en0, u_sync_en1), each with STAGES=2.
  DFF type is $_DFF_PN0_ (positive-edge clock, negative-level async reset).
- All 2 latches are INTENTIONAL: they form the core of the ICG cells
  (u_icg0, u_icg1), ensuring enable signals only change when the respective
  clock is low, preventing runt pulses on the gated clock outputs.
- Yosys inferred $_DLATCH_P_ (positive-enable transparent latch) because
  the RTL uses `if (!clk)` which becomes active when clk=0 (negative level).
  The latch enable is the inverted clock, so the latch is transparent
  during the low phase of each clock.
- The feedback interlock (en0_raw = ~sel & ~en1_sync, en1_raw = sel & ~en0_sync)
  ensures break-before-make switching even when sel changes asynchronously.
